A||||5||LivoniaFieroGT||air scoops for the GT||||1||
Z||000000||LivoniaFieroGT||05-02-2001||03:09 PM||||WTB a set of the over the hood air scoops for a GT.  Saw one and think I'd like to install.  They appear to come out of the louvers and up over the side quarter glass.  Can they be ducted to the airbox?||||reg||1
Z||000001||TOM||05-02-2001||06:19 PM||||Those double roof scoops basically defeat the whole air flow through a fiero engine bay. The air comes up off the road and through the trunk scoops. With those things you try to ram air down through the vents. I have heard from a reputable source that they make it run hotter as they stall the air in the bay.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||05-02-2001||08:26 PM||||search the forums. including the archives. several people who put the scoops in aren't happy. Rear visibility is bad to begin with. the scoops make it worse.||||reg||1
Z||000003||LivoniaFieroGT||05-02-2001||08:36 PM||||Thanks... since heat is my major concern because of the auto trans and I want a trans cooler..... I'll pass to another option....any ideas?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||05-02-2001||09:11 PM||||You can get the side scoops that replace the lower panels between the doors and rear tires or an Fiero Indy Scoop. (Like I have)<BR>It blows air down the backside of the engine. That way the grates still draw air up the front and the scoop pushes down the back creating constant air flow.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/All_pics_1.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 05-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||pontiacs4me||05-03-2001||02:17 AM||||When I install the 3800 in mine I plan to find a 12 volt fan that is about 12 inches across, something like a radiator fan, and put one under each rear engine vent,  to help push air out, primarialy at idle.  And I will have side scoops, etc etc.  A guy that owns a local machine shop told me that 3800's in fiero engine bays create alot of heat, so I think this will help.  My .02 ||||reg||1
